IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Rules of the Supreme Court 1971 (WA) -- the date arithmetic the rules need: Order 3 (time) and Order 68 r. 5 (the days
-- the Central Office is open), kept in one small module so that daydate is imported in one place only.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates`

-- A calendar date, day first.
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` d m y MEANS Date d m y

GIVEN x IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day n days after` x n MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL x PLUS n)

-- How many days from the first date to the second (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` a b MEANS DATE_SERIAL b MINUS DATE_SERIAL a

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later date of` a b MEANS
    IF `days from` a b GREATER THAN 0
    THEN b
    ELSE a

§§ `Months (O. 3 r. 1: a month is a calendar month)`

-- The date n calendar months on from x, on the same day of the month; where that month has no such day, the date rolls
-- into the next month (Date 30 2 2027 is 2 March 2027), and the caller takes the last day of the month instead.
GIVEN x IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the same day n months on from` x n MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY x) `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `the months counted` MEANS DATE_MONTH x MINUS 1 PLUS n
        `the year` MEANS DATE_YEAR x PLUS FLOOR (`the months counted` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the month` MEANS (`the months counted` MODULO 12) PLUS 1

GIVEN x IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the month n months on has the same day` x n IF
    DATE_DAY (`the same day n months on from` x n) EQUALS DATE_DAY x

-- The last day of a period of n calendar months beginning with day x (the day x itself counted): the day before the
-- day numerically corresponding to x, n months on; where there is no such day, the last day of that month (fork F3).
GIVEN x IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of n months beginning with` x n MEANS
    IF `the month n months on has the same day` x n
    THEN `the day n days after` (`the same day n months on from` x n) (0 MINUS 1)
    ELSE `the day n days after` (`the same day n months on from` x n) (0 MINUS (DATE_DAY (`the same day n months on from` x n)))

-- The last day of a period of n calendar months after day x (O. 3 r. 2(1): day x itself excluded).
GIVEN x IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of n months after` x n MEANS
    `the last day of n months beginning with` (`the day n days after` x 1) n

§§ `O. 68 r. 5 -- the days the Central Office is closed`

-- Easter Sunday in year y (the Gregorian computus, anonymous algorithm).
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`Easter Sunday in` y MEANS
    Date `the day of the month` `the month of Easter` y
    WHERE
        a MEANS y MODULO 19
        b MEANS FLOOR (y DIVIDED BY 100)
        c MEANS y MODULO 100
        d MEANS FLOOR (b DIVIDED BY 4)
        e MEANS b MODULO 4
        f MEANS FLOOR ((b PLUS 8) DIVIDED BY 25)
        g MEANS FLOOR ((b MINUS f PLUS 1) DIVIDED BY 3)
        h MEANS ((19 TIMES a) PLUS b MINUS d MINUS g PLUS 15) MODULO 30
        i MEANS FLOOR (c DIVIDED BY 4)
        k MEANS c MODULO 4
        l MEANS (32 PLUS (2 TIMES e) PLUS (2 TIMES i) MINUS h MINUS k) MODULO 7
        mm MEANS FLOOR ((a PLUS (11 TIMES h) PLUS (22 TIMES l)) DIVIDED BY 451)
        `the sum` MEANS h PLUS l MINUS (7 TIMES mm) PLUS 114
        `the month of Easter` MEANS FLOOR (`the sum` DIVIDED BY 31)
        `the day of the month` MEANS (`the sum` MODULO 31) PLUS 1

GIVEN x IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Saturday or Sunday` x IF
        `Weekday of` x EQUALS 6
    OR  `Weekday of` x EQUALS 0

-- O. 68 r. 5: "The several offices of the Supreme Court shall be open on every day of the year, except Saturdays and
-- Sundays, Good Friday and Monday in Easter week, Christmas Day and all Public Service holidays." Public Service holidays
-- are not computed (fork F2): on such a day the answer here treats the office as open.
GIVEN x IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Central Office is closed on` x IF
        `a Saturday or Sunday` x
    OR  `days from` (`Easter Sunday in` (DATE_YEAR x)) x EQUALS (0 MINUS 2)
    OR  `days from` (`Easter Sunday in` (DATE_YEAR x)) x EQUALS 1
    OR  (DATE_DAY x EQUALS 25 AND DATE_MONTH x EQUALS 12)

§§ `O. 3 r. 3 -- 24 December to 15 January`

-- "the period or any part of the period which is between 24 December and 15 January next following shall not be
-- reckoned": both days taken as inside the period (fork F4).
GIVEN x IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `between 24 December and 15 January` x IF
        (DATE_MONTH x EQUALS 12 AND DATE_DAY x AT LEAST 24)
    OR  (DATE_MONTH x EQUALS 1 AND DATE_DAY x AT MOST 15)

§§ `O. 3 rr. 2-4 -- the last day of a period of days`

-- Whether a day counts towards a period: r. 2(2) drops days the Central Office is closed when fewer than 7 days are
-- prescribed; r. 3 drops 24 December to 15 January for a pleading or notice of appeal.
GIVEN x IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER, `a pleading step` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day is reckoned` x n `a pleading step` IF
        (NOT (n LESS THAN 7 AND `the Central Office is closed on` x))
    AND (NOT (`a pleading step` AND `between 24 December and 15 January` x))

-- Counting on from x until `left` reckoned days have passed.
GIVEN x IS A DATE, `left` IS A NUMBER, n IS A NUMBER, `a pleading step` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the day reached counting on from` x `left` n `a pleading step` MEANS
    IF `left` AT MOST 0
    THEN x
    ELSE IF `the day is reckoned` (`the day n days after` x 1) n `a pleading step`
         THEN `the day reached counting on from` (`the day n days after` x 1) (`left` MINUS 1) n `a pleading step`
         ELSE `the day reached counting on from` (`the day n days after` x 1) `left` n `a pleading step`

-- r. 4(1): a time expiring on a day the Central Office is closed is extended to the next day it is open, where the act
-- cannot be done on the closed day; r. 4(2): not for a document that must be filed electronically.
GIVEN x IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the next day the Central Office is open from` x MEANS
    IF `the Central Office is closed on` x
    THEN `the next day the Central Office is open from` (`the day n days after` x 1)
    ELSE x

-- The last day for an act to be done within n days after day x (not clear days): r. 2(1) excludes day x and includes
-- the last day; r. 2(2) and r. 3 drop days as above; r. 4 extends a last day on which the office is closed when the act
-- needs the office open.
GIVEN x IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER, `a pleading step` IS A BOOLEAN, `needs the office open` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`O. 3 -- the last day of n days after` x n `a pleading step` `needs the office open` MEANS
    IF `needs the office open`
    THEN `the next day the Central Office is open from` `the counted day`
    ELSE `the counted day`
    WHERE
        `the counted day` MEANS `the day reached counting on from` x n n `a pleading step`
